+## Retry-After
+
+If the error an attempt throws has a numeric `retryAfter` property (in seconds), for example one set from a `429` response's `Retry-After` header, that time is **added** to the normal backoff delay before the next attempt. It is added rather than replacing the backoff so that many clients released at the same moment are still spread out; use `randomize: true` for that to work. `maxTimeout` caps only the backoff part. The sleep is still cut short by `maxRetryTime`, and a value that is not a positive finite number is ignored. The combined delay is reported as `retryDelay`.
+
 ## Tip
 
 You can pass arguments to the function being retried by wrapping it in an inline arrow function:
